          "id": "http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300435416",
          "type": "Type",
          "_label": "Details (Official List Description)"
        }
      ],
      "content": "SP 9211 11/56 TRING CHURCH YARD (South side) War Memorial GV II War memorial. Circa 1920. Limestone with knapped flint panels in 2 piers at ends of wrought iron railing on S in-line with graveyard wall. A tall carved stone cross standing in the graveyard facing S.  Base of 3 octagonal steps with inscribed names,  square top  step with relief lettering in panels, large inscribed socket block with chamfered corners and top, tall tapering shaft carved with running vine scroll down the angles, octagonal moulded cap and crucifix with octagonal boss terminals to cross. Octagonal moulded caps to square piers to each end of gap formed in graveyard wall. Listing NGR: SP9245811447 This List entry has been amended to add sources for War Memorials Online and the War Memorials Register. These sources were not used in the compilation of this List entry but are added here as a guide for further reading, 13 March 2017."
    }
  ],
